From c08edb0653c2e9052f2e5edc82f62ab8851843bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nigel Todman <veritas@vts-tech.org>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:36:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vkwhy: name the Vulkan fallback, keep -shader authoritative

The always-SDL2 mystery had three layers, all now closed:

- libslang-vk M4.05 had bugs that failed the Vulkan path on real
  drivers; M4.06 (pinned at 09068b25) fixes them.
- When the path does fall back, the game never said why: every
  failure exit of I_VK_AttemptGraphics now records a human-readable
  reason, shown in the stats overlay's shader row ('crt.slangp
  (unused: preset failed to load)') and echoed to stdout ('Vulkan
  path inactive (...) - classic renderer'). stderr is invisible in
  Windows GUI builds - exactly where fallbacks bite hardest.
- A -novulkan run persists usevulkan = 0; later -shader <path> runs
  then silently stayed classic. -shader on the command line is
  explicit intent and now re-enables the path (and persists 1);
  -novulkan still wins when both are given.

Also: vcpkg.json requests sdl2[vulkan] (the vulkan feature is not
in vcpkg's sdl2 defaults, so MSVC artifacts linked an SDL2 that
could never present), the CMake pin comment now matches the M4.06
git-commit-hash pin, and README-VK/CHANGELOG document all of it.

Verified on Xvfb + lavapipe (scripts/vkwhy_test.sh): 17/17 -
fallback reasons named and overlay-visible, -shader re-enable +
persistence through graceful quit, -novulkan precedence,
-vkcapture channel regression, M4.06 Vulkan path active.
